WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Organisms make shells and skeletons that accumulate as carbonate

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.660
sediment. Warm, clear, shallow water can support reefs. Tiny

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.900
carbonate skeletons can form chalk; recognizable shell fragments can

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.420
form coquina. Both differ from clastic quartz sand. Agitated

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.820
shallow water rolls grains while carbonate precipitates around them.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.180
Repeated coatings form ooids. Watch the coatings grow around

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.220
a moving nucleus. Magnesium-bearing fluids can later change carbonate

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.320
mineralogy to dolomite. As saline water evaporates, dissolved minerals

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.360
can precipitate as evaporites. In a saturated wetland, plant

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.480
material can survive decay and become coal through burial.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.260
Identify composition and formation pathway together; nonclastic rocks do

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.880
not share one single origin.
